## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design non-intrusive monitoring in KCNA, track per-partition state, and emit reliable alerts without affecting throughput.

## Key Concepts
- Per-partition lag tracking
- End offsets vs committed offsets
- Non-intrusive monitoring
- Idempotent alerting and deduplication

## Code Example
```javascript
class LagMonitor {
  constructor(threshold, windowMs = 60000) {
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.windowMs = windowMs;
    this.lagMap = new Map();
    this.lastAlert = new Map();
  }
  onMessage(partition, endOffset, committedOffset) {
    const lag = endOffset - committedOffset;
    const now = Date.now();
    this.lagMap.set(partition, { lag, ts: now });
    this.check(partition);
  }
  check(partition) {
    const entry = this.lagMap.get(partition);
    if (!entry) return;
    if (entry.lag > this.threshold && (Date.now() - entry.ts) >= this.windowMs) {
      this.emitAlert(partition, entry.lag);
      this.lastAlert.set(partition, Date.now());
      // reset timer for next alert window
      this.lagMap.set(partition, { lag: entry.lag, ts: Date.now() });
    }
  }
  emitAlert(partition, lag) {
    // publish to 'lag_alerts' with partition, lag, timestamp, host
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for dynamic partitions or multiple topics?
- How would you test alerting under network jitter and partitions rebalance?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of windowed stream processing, stateful aggregations with TTL management, and idempotent output semantics—all critical concepts for reliable event-driven systems.

## Key Concepts
- **Windowing**: Groups time-series events into fixed intervals (tumbling windows) for aggregate computation
- **Per-user state with TTL**: Maintains isolated metrics per user, automatically expiring stale entries to bound memory usage
- **Idempotent outputs**: Ensures deterministic results so duplicate processing (from restarts or retries) produces the same output

## Code Example
```javascript
class WindowedCTR {
  constructor(windowSizeMs = 5000, ttlMs = 60000) {
    this.windowSizeMs = windowSizeMs;
    this.ttlMs = ttlMs;
    this.state = new Map();
  }

  processMessage(msg) {
    const { userId, type, timestamp } = JSON.parse(msg.value);
    const windowStart = Math.floor(timestamp / this.windowSizeMs) * this.windowSizeMs;
    const key = `${userId}:${windowStart}`;

    if (!this.state.has(key)) {
      this.state.set(key, { clicks: 0, impressions: 0, emitted: false, lastUpdate: Date.now() });
    }
    const window = this.state.get(key);
    if (type === 'click') window.clicks++;
    if (type === 'impression') window.impressions++;
    window.lastUpdate = Date.now();

    if (!window.emitted && Date.now() - windowStart >= this.windowSizeMs) {
      this.emitCTR(key, window);
      window.emitted = true;
    }
  }

  commitOffsets(offsets) { /* persist consumer offsets */ }
  windowState() { return Array.from(this.state.entries()); }
}
```

